{"id":"H0621","lemma":"אָֽסְנַת","transliteration":"asenat","sayIt":"a-se-NAT","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"Asenath","meaning":"A woman living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.41.45;\ndaughter of: Potiphera (H6319); married to Joseph (H3130);\nmother of: Manasseh (H4519) and Ephraim (H0669)\n§ Asenath = \"belonging to the goddess Neith\"\nthe wife of Joseph","glosses":["asenath"],"count":3,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"gen-41","v":45,"renderings":{"bsb":"Asenath","kjv":"Asenath"}},{"chapterId":"gen-41","v":50,"renderings":{"bsb":"by Asenath","kjv":"which Asenath"}},{"chapterId":"gen-46","v":20,"renderings":{"bsb":"by Asenath","kjv":"which Asenath"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Genesis 41:45","note":"Pharaoh called Joseph’s name Zaphenath-Paneah. He gave him Asenath, the daughter of Potiphera priest of On as a wife. Joseph went out over the land of Egypt.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H6319","lemma":"פּוֹטִי פֶ֫רַע","transliteration":"poti phera","gloss":"Potiphera"},{"id":"H3130","lemma":"יוֹסֵף","transliteration":"yoseph","gloss":"Joseph"},{"id":"H4519","lemma":"מְנַשֶּׁה","transliteration":"menashsheh","gloss":"Manasseh"},{"id":"H0669","lemma":"אֶפְרַ֫יִם","transliteration":"ephrayim","gloss":"Ephraim"},{"id":"H0673","lemma":"אֶפְרָתִי","transliteration":"ephrati","gloss":"Ephraimite"},{"id":"H3084","lemma":"יְהוֹסֵף","transliteration":"yehoseph","gloss":"Joseph"},{"id":"H4520","lemma":"מְנַשִּׁי","transliteration":"menashshi","gloss":"Manassite"},{"id":"H6085","lemma":"עֶפְרוֹן","transliteration":"ephron","gloss":"Ephron"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}